module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_field_read_on_an_unestablished_element_type_is_accepted_through_its_slot

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CeilingNotStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_field_read_on_an_unestablished_element_type_is_accepted_through_its_slot: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_field_read_on_an_unestablished_element_type_is_accepted_through_its_slot" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: CeilingNotStated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a value whose element type no one established -- a List typed by an empty `[]` literal, whose element slot holds the inference placeholder TypeVariable(empty_list_element) -- reaches a field read through a generic callee's lambda, and v1.compiler.infer ACCEPTS the read whether or not any record declares the field. The guard written for exactly this case (is_never_constrained_enclosing_generic_base: deferring a read of empty_list_element 'would accept a field of a type nobody established') never sees it, because the substitution binds the callee's type variable to the application's element SLOT node, which is not itself a type variable.",
    "SPECIMEN (seed built from main 557a7efac39, bold-koi-381, 2026-10-25, gunbc compile --entry on fixture modules): `type Row { tags: List<String> }`, local generics `fl<T, A>(xs: List<T>, empty: A, cons: fn(A, T) -> A) -> A` and `snoc<T>(xs: List<T>, item: T) -> List<T>`; `let rows = fl(xs: xs, empty: [], cons: fn(acc, r) { snoc(xs: acc, item: r) })` then `fl(xs: rows, empty: 0, cons: fn(n, r) { n + length(xs: r.nope) })` -- `nope` is declared by nothing -- compiles with no blocking diagnostic (it stops only at the emitted-workspace write). DISCRIMINATING CONTROL: the same module with `let rows: List<Row> = ..` REFUSES the read (1 blocking error). The declared field `r.tags` through the unannotated let compiles. In the corpus: the same shape at v2.compiler.source_root_eval (modules = fold_list(xs: sources, empty: [], ..), then m.declarations / m.module / m.path) and v2.compiler.type_declaration_use_census (edge.label / edge.target) -- nine reads accepted on main whose element type is the placeholder.",
    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5) -- an undeclared field read is Accepted, and nothing refuses until the emitted target compiles or the value is consumed.",
    "HOW IT SURFACED: gunbc#15132's first head made unify_generic_child_pairs bind the slot's held type instead of the slot; the placeholder then reached the guard, which refused all nine corpus reads, and v2-bootstrap failed at emit (job 121128203061). The reads are not wrong programs -- their element type IS established by the fold's cons step -- so the corpus is correct and the seed has never typed them: on main they pass for the wrong reason.",
    "ROOT, per keen-heron-809's sequencing: v1.compiler.infer unify_generics binds a type variable FIRST-WINS, so the uninformative placeholder from `empty: []` takes the binding and the informative actual that follows (the cons step's item) never does. smart-tern-402's seed PR is the repair: an actual whose held type is an inference variable never takes a binding, and the first informative actual replaces one that holds it (the fold-accumulator class, heal E0282 on #15115). With that landed, the reads above are typed at their real element type, and an undeclared one refuses at the guard as intended.",
    "V2 VERDICT (same source through v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation bla_assemble_with_peers then v2.compiler.infer infer, bold-koi-381, 2026-10-25): v2 FAILS CLOSED -- the undeclared read refuses as infer_reason_projection_receiver_declares_no_fields and the annotated control as infer_reason_field_not_declared_on_receiver, so v2 carries no silent acceptance. It also refuses the DECLARED read through the unannotated let (projection_receiver_declares_no_fields): v2 types the accumulator at the empty literal's element and does not refine it from the cons step, a false refusal of the same fold-accumulator shape. It is fail-closed and KNOWN, not a new hole: the same gap as an unannotated lambda or accumulator whose type is fixed only by an uninformative init (stern-cat-126's handoff of gunbc#15038, open item 2), and it stays at the mitigatable rung until that unification lands -- its trigger, not a separate row.",
    "RELATED CLASSES, one placeholder and distinct invalid states: gunbc.recurring_failure_mode unsolved_placeholder_reads_back_as_unit is the same empty_list_element placeholder reaching a field read that REFUSES but names Unit (a misattributed refusal, where this row is a silent acceptance); gunbc.recurring_failure_mode unapplied_generic_accumulator_types_element_as_container is the fold accumulator read off an unapplied expansion. The shared link is the fold carrier fixed by an uninformative init: gunbc#15022 (bright-pike-492) closes an open carrier, [] included, at the step's produced type in the seed, and gunbc#14411 records the first-wins reading of the same placeholder. Whichever of those lands is this row's next-rung trigger, re-measured with this specimen.",
    "CEILING NOT STATED: a field read whose receiver type is an unsolved inference variable is decidable at the read; the next rung is the first-wins repair above plus an enrolled RED (this specimen's undeclared read refusing) with the declared-field positive control.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "unify_generics"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.infer", decl_name: "is_never_constrained_enclosing_generic_base"),
  ],
}
